\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,1),(4,-1),(-3,-5).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2af2881-a673-5b57-bd3a-7b0a0c5b9c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465273} {:answer/id #uuid "c5fbbe59-f0e2-5ee8-aafd-3b934b1b4ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5fbbe59-f0e2-5ee8-aafd-3b934b1b4ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465274} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bae1bf3-33e4-529f-8225-d16d80ad6410" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466480} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ae369b-d1e0-5cc4-abd5-07b211cf5919" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465275} {:answer/id #uuid "a987fc9f-5e71-51cd-943f-f07a66df7ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a987fc9f-5e71-51cd-943f-f07a66df7ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465276} :answer-field/id #uuid "39f6dcc6-ba6c-5182-9aa5-5100a1798744" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466481} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86a4bbf2-72bc-5426-9a60-6c05feff0aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465277} {:answer/id #uuid "0fffb888-8aef-5e2f-9d5b-43914e12c6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fffb888-8aef-5e2f-9d5b-43914e12c6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465278} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9e85ba9-10cb-5eb1-aa1c-410baea17cfc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff0f96a5-d30c-508e-bdde-b67be8bf18d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-160374" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(4,-3),(2,-2),(1,3).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(-4,3)$\n- **II.** $(-2,2)$\n- **III.** $(-1,-3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians is the same as counterclockwise rotation by the same angle. It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-\\pi },$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-4,3),(-2,2),(-1,-3).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4b612ef-ce7f-5783-848d-d8ef210c9f47" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Argand Diagram Corresponding to a Complex Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4429b43-58be-5f07-b740-2eac2b1e9ce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465279} {:answer/id #uuid "ae9ca6ba-0e5e-570a-9451-2e8ef0de4c1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4429b43-58be-5f07-b740-2eac2b1e9ce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465279} :answer-field/id #uuid "de898eb9-cd87-5988-bfe1-596e26f3fa41" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466483} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b03aca7-961f-578d-9808-ec98c36135ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465281} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7ff91b-cd93-506d-b5f7-0dae15c563c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b03aca7-961f-578d-9808-ec98c36135ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465281} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c85ab09-81cb-5c1d-b7df-a151083686be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466484} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57b0741b-4b42-5ac2-a2e4-71b7dd123a3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465283} {:answer/id #uuid "020635f5-70f2-5d39-8e15-e543547d6ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "020635f5-70f2-5d39-8e15-e543547d6ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465284} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4216041-9c14-562f-8c91-9269e914faea" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0ef2dcb7-ec09-542d-a947-352534dabf78" :question/math-academy-id "q-160399" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers lie in the fourth quadrant in an Argand diagram?\n- **I.** $3+4\\text{i}$\n- **II.** $-2+3\\text{i}$\n- **III.** $1-2\\text{i}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The complex number $3+4\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=3$ and the imaginary part $y=4.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(3,4)$, which lies in the first quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-2+3\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-2$ and the imaginary part $y=3.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-2,3)$, which lies in the second quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $1-2\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=1$ and the imaginary part $y=-2.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(1,-2)$, which lies in the fourth quadrant.\n\n![](images/a4/a4f87e680d46b099b9543b552191c776ac7145fba4e1b51b10c44a3685907d46.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a6ca425-0e94-5b83-8729-fda13fbf3d7d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equilibrium Solutions of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10fbd1fd-81d6-5ab9-9a42-0df9f96eda22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465285} {:answer/id #uuid "1395580a-0ad4-5646-9291-c0acb3fea193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10fbd1fd-81d6-5ab9-9a42-0df9f96eda22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465285} :answer-field/id #uuid "84ac4b21-d3c8-5ac0-b070-d7d504bcc850" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466486} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccfd9b16-57d1-5331-8023-5fa2705b3253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465287} {:answer/id #uuid "047f3772-89f4-5fce-a998-333acb699eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccfd9b16-57d1-5331-8023-5fa2705b3253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465287} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b2cdc27-e594-5f5c-81a3-b5b4ae2af15d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466487} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1f86228-76ce-5ad6-8dba-2e38cc396dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465289} {:answer/id #uuid "f3293a37-b3c5-57c9-8cd2-7bebc9961197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3293a37-b3c5-57c9-8cd2-7bebc9961197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465290} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6eadc1-e12f-5563-a5fe-c1f034620e4e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c7b0ec58-a026-543f-8622-101c6f9cdc96" :question/math-academy-id "q-160419" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\pi .$ Which of the following is an equilibrium solution of this equation?\n- **I.** $y=0$\n- **II.** $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n- **III.** $y=\\pi $\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given an autonomous differential equation ${y}^{′}(t)=f(y),$ if there exists a constant $c$ such that $f(c)=0,$ then $y=c$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation.\n\nFirst, we write the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-y+\\pi ,\n$$\n\nand we get that $f(y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-y+\\pi .$\n\nNow, let's check each proposed solution by substituting them into $f(y).$\n\n- $y=0$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(0)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-0+\\pi =\\pi \\ne 0.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi =1+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\ne 0.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $y=\\pi $ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(\\pi )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\pi +\\pi =0-\\pi +\\pi =0.$$\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a6ca425-0e94-5b83-8729-fda13fbf3d7d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equilibrium Solutions of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53189a57-4a52-569c-b4e6-971a16c99c31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465291} {:answer/id #uuid "2ffce523-690d-5d3f-ade2-3f244c6d6161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ffce523-690d-5d3f-ade2-3f244c6d6161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465292} :answer-field/id #uuid "247493c4-7128-51e9-9e5c-5ea79e484ddb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466489} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c7feaaa-a4a2-57fb-b6b2-dfc3fcb0aa5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465293} {:answer/id #uuid "b59ae2a3-7e6e-513d-95bd-ba5c448d88bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b59ae2a3-7e6e-513d-95bd-ba5c448d88bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465294} :answer-field/id #uuid "51ca2add-20e1-5ed3-9359-fea868180b27" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466490} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceec5708-f222-5686-b123-0c46ad5f48b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465295} {:answer/id #uuid "fb17ae72-76f4-5cdd-9d25-d53e0e9875f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceec5708-f222-5686-b123-0c46ad5f48b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465295} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8f19a1b-9d84-5e40-900d-78c7d390c63f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09328241-3b39-5707-a62b-8ca38e3a3a9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-160422" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=1.$ Which of the following is an equilibrium solution of this equation?\n- **I.** $y=-1$\n- **II.** $y=1$\n- **III.** $y=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given an autonomous differential equation ${y}^{′}(x)=f(y),$ if there exists a constant $c$ such that $f(c)=0,$ then $y=c$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation.\n\nFirst, we write the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand we get that $f(y)=1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}.$\n\nNow, let's check each proposed solution by substituting them into $f(y).$\n\n- $y=-1$ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(-1)=1-\\frac{1}{(-1)^{2}}=1-1=0.$$\\,✓$\n\n- $y=1$ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(1)=1-\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}=1-1=0.$$\\,✓$\n\n- $y=2$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(2)=1-\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}}=\\frac{3}{4}\\ne 0.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "398c4cf2-b5b9-558d-832b-37f666218d96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465297} {:answer/id #uuid "412b77ef-dc77-580c-befa-7e9379a921e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "412b77ef-dc77-580c-befa-7e9379a921e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465298} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a10b74b-d355-5da6-b34a-57def74627a4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466492} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8526823d-abcc-54bf-8af4-da58bb047c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465299} {:answer/id #uuid "aec99e2a-8eb4-58b4-9590-18a02351b254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8526823d-abcc-54bf-8af4-da58bb047c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465299} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e8b78d8-7d38-52f4-ad95-3cc927aa6e15" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466493} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "901b8d79-bea7-584b-99ca-ebc77ca52742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465301} {:answer/id #uuid "bcdc5504-5f38-536f-9b87-1ee4610cde1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "901b8d79-bea7-584b-99ca-ebc77ca52742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465301} :answer-field/id #uuid "1622fd27-1eaf-55b1-b8a8-b142061f2303" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b24e08c4-4299-5d2f-a3af-dcce0689b7c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-160447" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x/2},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\le 0,$ we have $f(x)={e}^{x/2}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{e}^{x/2}\\,{|}_{-\\infty }^{0} \\\\  & =2({e}^{0}-0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8574032e-7d34-5165-a4e0-00628f417667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465303} {:answer/id #uuid "7c831406-c2c1-5a56-b6e8-99b724d7c7fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c831406-c2c1-5a56-b6e8-99b724d7c7fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465304} :answer-field/id #uuid "b968f63e-b65b-5762-920c-5c39cf8c5680" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466495} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d474bfd9-08af-50f8-a009-ffd1c5fa29a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465305} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9e254d-304a-5fcb-ba2e-abddfc9762b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d474bfd9-08af-50f8-a009-ffd1c5fa29a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465305} :answer-field/id #uuid "580e15f7-7c9b-5b5b-b207-504cf71ede08" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60289d96-5d64-506a-bb60-39aea93ffe10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465307} {:answer/id #uuid "cc49bedf-8d39-5a9a-b0c5-310023c19458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60289d96-5d64-506a-bb60-39aea93ffe10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465307} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1b0fc18-cd28-52cf-a80e-e991e6040ca2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0b61c31-2e3e-5b9a-9684-a3b763cdba2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-160450" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3afe07d2-ac9e-5cf3-a0df-a60fba1947a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465309} {:answer/id #uuid "39b9a9e2-b274-59d1-a806-fb760cfa292c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39b9a9e2-b274-59d1-a806-fb760cfa292c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465310} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7a9fb37-814f-59d8-98df-cf807c43024a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466498} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "785644ac-003f-5ff6-bd02-b0063c3522f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465311} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e4e5d1-4b09-51f4-9dc6-03ca0eac53c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "785644ac-003f-5ff6-bd02-b0063c3522f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465311} :answer-field/id #uuid "7670715a-8a93-5131-b8d0-47fc4afd8030" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466499} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4cbbe22-5b0a-5c75-9b19-864b6a6135d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465313} {:answer/id #uuid "37c1c95c-f41d-553a-a794-3684167e0740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4cbbe22-5b0a-5c75-9b19-864b6a6135d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465313} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7db66c4-37dd-5377-b424-3bc72a80a6f1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9f1f757-0f29-5257-92da-0c605e690da7" :question/math-academy-id "q-160455" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{1-2x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=2{e}^{1-2x}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }2{e}^{1-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-2x}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a5b2ba9-1bfe-57b5-9caf-c99e7cd00766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465315} {:answer/id #uuid "0e47c71f-651b-5dab-adbd-31cee6b0d544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a5b2ba9-1bfe-57b5-9caf-c99e7cd00766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465315} :answer-field/id #uuid "81d1cd43-a1b8-500d-ac08-e5f0fb4d4fe8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96cce611-53f4-585e-abe8-9b124fe8324e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465317} {:answer/id #uuid "6aae8e41-20a4-5fa6-a286-626b3ae6f630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6aae8e41-20a4-5fa6-a286-626b3ae6f630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465318} :answer-field/id #uuid "b37cfc2c-cedf-5629-9c08-1c82f0317e43" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466502} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8081da32-5615-591d-a668-9527b67107cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465319} {:answer/id #uuid "7537192a-f28a-5528-8449-0c72e08da197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8081da32-5615-591d-a668-9527b67107cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465319} :answer-field/id #uuid "14279bd7-1c43-5024-8057-80e3b4ec2a59" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61d3fab2-038b-5d24-9a0c-708feb5787d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160617" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,1),(-1,2),(1,2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians about the origin?\n- **I.** $(1,1)$\n- **II.** $(1,-2)$\n- **III.** $(-1,3)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by an angle of $\\pi $ radians is the same as counterclockwise rotation by the same angle. It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-\\pi },$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-\\pi }$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(0,-1),(1,-2),(-1,-2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092224 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20f4ef93-3e7b-58ec-992e-3a62b12b74e2" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 180 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12754a27-cfb2-59a0-a8a9-3ab89e93f58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465321} {:answer/id #uuid "57965a7a-f55b-516a-b0cb-e1a7de6d4bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57965a7a-f55b-516a-b0cb-e1a7de6d4bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465322} :answer-field/id #uuid "8da0c5d0-f939-52d8-aa0f-9bd7ecb473e8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466504} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b26ef560-cffb-5f08-8abc-7890adc70746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465323} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4ad11c-95b9-5ec4-8db8-8aced9