0).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n- **I.** $(-1,3)$\n- **II.** $(4,1)$\n- **III.** $(0,-1)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{90}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,-3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,\\,-4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{90}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\,-3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\,\\,\\,-4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-1,-3),(4,1),(0,1).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25472444-965c-56bd-af48-3f4e5133b252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465345} {:answer/id #uuid "5356ea59-9f04-5828-9613-d1148be9ac96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5356ea59-9f04-5828-9613-d1148be9ac96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text