eave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the top side.\n\nFor the top side, we have $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{5}.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})),\\,0\\le u\\le \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/b8/b836799bc512db70d2ce5fcfe70db2af3b2572d584d317fa5ed515b363a11ddc.png)\n\n \n\nNote that the line that this segment lies on passes through the origin. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. The slope of the line is\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nAs a result, our line makes an angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ radians with the positive $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement III is false.\n\n- When $u=0,$ we obtain the point $(0,\\,0),$ which is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane.\n\n- When $u=\\sqrt{5},$ we obtain the point \n$(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}),\\,\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})),$\nwhose distance to $O$ is $\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nSo, one endpoint of the segment is the origin $O$ of the $xy$-plane, while the other endpoint lies in the circle with radius $\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $O.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c05d4f9-eb1b-59a1-ae0b-5d6869bad7c5" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dc900d5-6adb-5291-bb29-945c24e8a52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465375} {:answer/id #uuid "c5db8b48-0145-59b3-853e-2dc9a73f5319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dc900d5-6adb-5291-bb29-945c24e8a52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465375} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ba930a6-1b15-54d9-9b76-147214cfd918" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466531} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86f9f9d7-6a29-54a0-b78d-ab1ada5cb3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465377} {:answer/id #uuid "66070404-2e4d-59d0-81b6-d80fbc47cbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66070404-2e4d-59d0-81b6-d80fbc47cbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465378} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e459526-4e2e-5b5d-9c5a-53a2552e46e3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43c5d968-0c47-5b5c-af0a-2a7a009a838c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465379} {:answer/id #uuid "bf8627ef-3c0a-5dbb-bc99-ce2b4f5f165f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43c5d968-0c47-5b5c-af0a-2a7a009a838c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465379} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4d526b-c9a0-5573-a72d-651b90ac9856" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b05250a-2126-54a5-8110-d92f7f2aa122" :question/math-academy-id "q-161117" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7bb6d2b9f9e09de44e078657ce3517bfd78261d3206743b7882abf0112f38a93.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $x=0$, $x=1$, $y=0$, $y=1$, $z=0,$ and $z=3-x+y.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(x,y)\\le z\\le {f}_{2}(x,y)}\n$$\n\n \nas a type I region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}$\n- ${f}_{1}(x,y)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=3-x+y$\n- ${f}_{1}(x,y)=1$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=4$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type I region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/05/05f940e247c6cd5d862d81fc3a34658353bef5513dfe862bbc67a120c0345838.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $xy$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Indeed, we have\n\n- the *bottom* surface $z={f}_{1}(x,y)=0$, and\n\n- the *top* surface $z={f}_{2}(x,y)=3-x+y.$\n\n![](images/65/65e179e16b66009b9168c4380032b01c3a79b3c4a2afc3b8e5084defb77b85fc.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278389 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c05d4f9-eb1b-59a1-ae0b-5d6869bad7c5" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cabb0a8d-aff4-57ab-96f0-f8d0915a925d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465381} {:answer/id #uuid "6578be7a-a203-5728-8f45-7417f3a0a68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6578be7a-a203-5728-8f45-7417f3a0a68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465382} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7df53d5-584d-50cd-959b-c1935fb43d75" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76e10513-2430-594e-8305-5bb7ccc10a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465383} {:answer/id #uuid "5beefa76-4a9e-5425-8ae8-78a4b372ea51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76e10513-2430-594e-8305-5bb7ccc10a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465383} :answer-field/id #uuid "697d5114-f05b-5010-aa74-40202b0c59b3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79f1e02b-e929-5dcd-8dd3-1c7a56b7b8b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465385} {:answer/id #uuid "61410729-3c43-570c-9bd4-40124d7efd17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79f1e02b-e929-5dcd-8dd3-1c7a56b7b8b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465385} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b954c2f-713e-5e8c-9abc-b9a072f0f21c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "99aeb9ca-3424-5f18-af86-89763375eaeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161125" :question/problem "![](images/e5/e5369264a9ab9328449bafd6fd3dcda1a70b7d90cbaf4f9815211e0cc3873fc0.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $x=0$, $x=3$, $y=0$, $y=2$, $z=0,$ and $4x+5z=15.$ Given its representation\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(x,y)\\le z\\le {f}_{2}(x,y)}\n$$\n\n \nas a type I region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}$\n- ${f}_{1}(x,y)=2$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=\\frac{15-4x}{5}$\n- ${f}_{1}(x,y)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=3$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type I region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/05/05f940e247c6cd5d862d81fc3a34658353bef5513dfe862bbc67a120c0345838.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $xy$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II and statement III are false. We have\n\n- the *bottom* surface $z={f}_{1}(x,y)=0$, and\n\n- the *top* surface $z={f}_{2}(x,y)=\\frac{15-4x}{5}.$\n\n![](images/ed/edea8af334c3362f583fcb86709150690eeec79a54185b67d242bfa14a8e4c75.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcc1bf5-5eea-5615-8b16-b8ced5de7984" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a5de68-5950-514f-9ba1-08fa9d4299ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465387} {:answer/id #uuid "99ded4e4-29f1-558a-9986-b3ec79c00a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99ded4e4-29f1-558a-9986-b3ec79c00a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465388} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcb986ee-74d8-55e7-ace6-4c46cc82d2fa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805d79bd-85e2-5be6-930c-9af401f32ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465389} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc276e3-6d65-585e-9956-fe2637e49b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "805d79bd-85e2-5be6-930c-9af401f32ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465389} :answer-field/id #uuid "845a991c-16c1-5dca-bbbc-d4f135e22f63" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e54cac66-bf9d-526e-b2f2-c9397de7dc54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465391} {:answer/id #uuid "328852b4-a1a4-578a-9f26-a0109eec8aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e54cac66-bf9d-526e-b2f2-c9397de7dc54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465391} :answer-field/id #uuid "e14d9582-0fba-5cac-a562-27db433f61d6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83e332b2-7a45-565f-946e-09fe8f179dcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161247" :question/problem "![](images/60/60f622b161dbfb4da1d18e85d3eb3ab4e02c2af418f9845e05a3bf9704a28006.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $y=0$, $y=3$, $z=0$, $z=2$, $x=0,$ and $x=2+y-z.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {f}_{2}(y,z)}\n$$\n\n \nas a type II region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $D={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}$\n- ${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=2-y-z$\n- ${f}_{1}(y,z)=2+y-z$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=5$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e4/e4c9cbbad2f13e9cc125ddbb89125ed2d734eee3f80737125961f4af1846a972.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $yz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$\n\n- Statements II and III are false. We have\n\n- the *back* surface $x={f}_{1}(y,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *front* surface $x={f}_{2}(y,z)=2+y-z.$\n\n![](images/c2/c2af4029bd979d250ed15f351ef7f14d3ae688806db4ffec199a24b3591dadac.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dea8612-414c-5394-869d-1e404b048156" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type III Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b46cd556-9148-553e-a9ee-002da12838f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465393} {:answer/id #uuid "c81a3b20-2fa7-53cf-ba24-e30a9d7def19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c81a3b20-2fa7-53cf-ba24-e30a9d7def19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465394} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e938ae3-f27b-5e0d-93f6-fd7f5fbab6cf" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f9e2552-d78f-5856-897c-1066c7c11370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465395} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4fa949-854b-5ee7-8b85-75ab00ce9a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e4fa949-854b-5ee7-8b85-75ab00ce9a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465396} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ca3abf8-142e-5260-aec2-6a593434d8f3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2305890-a995-5d60-b9bd-dda89a17580d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465397} {:answer/id #uuid "85d5eb5f-70d4-55e0-9577-81a9d91ad5e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2305890-a995-5d60-b9bd-dda89a17580d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465397} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0610e88-6eb9-5b63-8129-a7376026d04c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d0077c3-5809-5281-a04f-def492b7900c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161248" :question/problem "![](images/40/40091bf7a66577a4a3f3b8cdf3b5da34cbe0e0198fdc5731c6d3dae8cb727418.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $x=0$, $x=1$, $z=0$, $z=3$, $y=0,$ and $y=4-z.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {f}_{2}(x,z)}\n$$\n\n \nas a type III region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $D={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}$\n- ${f}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=4-z$\n- ${f}_{1}(x,z)=4-z$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=4$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c3333ded3e00e7d7408f0dbd37807f1adec0301691cc6311871bfea6d7b9fa15.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $xz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. We have\n\n- the *left* surface $y={f}_{1}(x,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *right* surface $y={f}_{2}(x,z)=4-z.$\n\n![](images/b1/b1046e312a3783dfc3253646f8a71ae226a173ac882a6305850bdd81aed9dd7e.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dea8612-414c-5394-869d-1e404b048156" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type III Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87947aba-3ee6-5f0b-b3c6-cd6a066bd244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465399} {:answer/id #uuid "97174b7f-38ab-52ee-b9d8-8cb8b66d0e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97174b7f-38ab-52ee-b9d8-8cb8b66d0e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465400} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b5ae30f-59ec-58d7-a15c-4249798540d9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1ea4a1-1147-5bfc-8507-1bf0d77960ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465401} {:answer/id #uuid "f84ca98d-56b9-5e97-bfb2-dff3175e39ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c1ea4a1-1147-5bfc-8507-1bf0d77960ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465401} :answer-field/id #uuid "73340b15-0013-5823-988c-a3ba50461d3c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466544} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eae65db7-54ff-596a-b1e0-2327b0ecaba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465403} {:answer/id #uuid "23d0f29c-f34b-599c-8760-32746cd6d595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23d0f29c-f34b-599c-8760-32746cd6d595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465404} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cb2eb83-9dd5-5fd0-a343-cff27dd76ab1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9bbc7b8c-0af0-5315-ba58-db2c9cd43206" :question/math-academy-id "q-161250" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d447e5a00aa324d83a3f513db11ff677fd2db2c7b1b33d8bc2bcfa73b4a08f3f.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $x=0$, $x=3$, $z=0$, $z=2$, $y=0,$ and $y=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {f}_{2}(x,z)}\n$$\n\n \nas a type III region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $D={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}$\n- ${f}_{1}(x,z)=z-\\frac{x}{3}$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3$\n- ${f}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c3333ded3e00e7d7408f0dbd37807f1adec0301691cc6311871bfea6d7b9fa15.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $xz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. We have\n\n- the *left* surface $y={f}_{1}(x,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *right* surface $y={f}_{2}(x,z)=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z.$\n\n![](images/88/88b5fde383f094436dd94adefa7912f1a194319739fdb0b8a6a9a74693362219.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278496 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcc1bf5-5eea-5615-8b16-b8ced5de7984" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "057db65a-eecb-52c7-ac69-c8a69baf0264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465405} {:answer/id #uuid "4640f754-7b8a-5863-a4a7-4984c1ec21a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4640f754-7b8a-5863-a4a7-4984c1ec21a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465406} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca4918c6-67e4-5f19-84fb-a1e03896cf0d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25c8e774-2be1-50a4-be88-195ee7a64ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465407} {:answer/id #uuid "450f49eb-7a8d-5ee5-80f1-0b4c034f20a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "450f49eb-7a8d-5ee5-80f1-0b4c034f20a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465408} :answer-field/id #uuid "bed649e4-9512-5df5-8690-508a27d9b3e5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "906a29e2-7f19-5c43-bd9f-25622a39d650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465409} {:answer/id #uuid "b1856245-617f-5aa9-b2a6-f6ea110eeb7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "906a29e2-7f19-5c43-bd9f-25622a39d650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465409} :answer-field/id #uuid "c51647d3-edd0-55aa-b2d7-68154b9214d2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59f1a985-1f99-5d8b-a66e-0643cac8da20" :question/math-academy-id "q-161361" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f7799ca5801bf019fc5b884590575346a8f298f8e9c91056c13a60c4dd23742d.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $y=0$, $y=4$, $z=0$, $z=3$, $x=0,$ and $x=4-y+2z.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {f}_{2}(y,z)}\n$$\n\n \nas a type II region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $D={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}$\n- ${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4-y+2z$\n- ${f}_{1}(y,z)=4+y-2z$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e4/e4c9cbbad2f13e9cc125ddbb89125ed2d734eee3f80737125961f4af1846a972.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $yz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true and statement III is false. We have\n\n- the *back* surface $x={f}_{1}(y,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *front* surface $x={f}_{2}(y,z)=4-y+2z.$\n\n![](images/3b/3bf8e141067fb6f675933f52e465114d8909d951f6ac85fb09c8dda7efbc2f38.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a024c46e-0374-5d03-b895-eb754ff7ad97" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Interiors and Boundaries of Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "769ab244-b50f-5cca-ab22-fd43c9447cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465411} {:answer/id #uuid "2c5149c3-ecba-57d2-b462-3dbdfb69933a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "769ab244-b50f-5cca-ab22-fd43c9447cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465411} :answer-field/id #uuid "087f9ca1-8165-5d08-815b-de98c18b98c3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466549} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61780875-68b1-505b-895f-12ff1ff66c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465413} {:answer/id #uuid "dad38122-7c39-50f3-9242-6e99cb69a4f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61780875-68b1-505b-895f-12ff1ff66c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465413} :answer-field/id #uuid "65372a61-77ce-559a-9860-6323bcc95b27" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466550} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0696dc0-2a39-515e-89a4-41b079d76ebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465415} {:answer/id #uuid "61f6634a-9066-5bbf-b0fc-703e680d6c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61f6634a-9066-5bbf-b0fc-703e680d6c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465416} :answer-field/id #uuid "db274c98-e65f-53ec-bc5e-861c8411a39d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be0484aa-ac87-5330-9ede-cd54e1386a15" :question/math-academy-id "q-161625" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ge 2-x\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\nII. $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nIII. $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/cd/cdca164d343d8bff4c78a1e366e52c588ca6c54dfdea61acea1900bcbdc79f31.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statements I and II are false. As we have seen, $A$ contains all its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains all of its boundary points, we must have $A-∂A⊊A.$ Therefore $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278576 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f462a13-e52b-5f50-bd9b-5e3e04a75ec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465417} {:answer/id #uuid "7d035b1f-7fbf-59ff-b61e-ebb312eee7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d035b1f-7fbf-59ff-b61e-ebb312eee7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465418} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4834f1a-3776-5597-bca0-28aea74896d7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4acc30dd-b0dd-5587-9188-4cc8367a69bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465419} {:answer/id #uuid "28f06c85-e623-54b7-9f55-9afd7009566f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28f06c85-e623-54b7-9f55-9afd7009566f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465420} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac548899-74b4-5b42-b1ca-0d1482e4229f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb0fe9bc-f78c-5c55-bbf7-fd65e2ea1195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465421} {:answer/id #uuid "c615d31d-cf76-5762-8eca-1a561a4f0997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb0fe9bc-f78c-5c55-bbf7-fd65e2ea1195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465421} :answer-field/id #uuid "28fa83d6-4600-547a-a25c-706ebb06a453" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fb05970-59dc-5904-9b90-0c1d735b4269" :question/math-academy-id "q-161638" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}\\le 3}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1<x<1,\\,0<y<2-{x}^{2}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1723e615-d467-58f5-999a-7973741641a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465423} {:answer/id #uuid "f9abc517-42f5-5df9-8763-751fa53ba7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1723e615-d467-58f5-999a-7973741641a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465423} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e72de96-4a0e-5793-9030-00840e107b1a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466555} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73751260-3c44-5990-85ed-3b267c03dae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465425} {:answer/id #uuid "370be496-358b-5e7b-a667-394d18ea293a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "370be496-358b-5e7b-a667-394d18ea293a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465426} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fb24073-6d92-542f-8596-ac6f6e4394df" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466556} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35f70d16-b32e-538c-9859-1005c1e1e446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465427} {:answer/id #uuid "35894513-fdab-5a3b-8565-fe3a1eae24b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35f70d16-b32e-538c-9859-1005c1e1e446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465427} :answer-field/id #uuid "41160ea6-dde2-54a9-aa26-dda3dbb64fc8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20984d3c-4813-50f9-a16b-ba04fcaf3833" :question/math-academy-id "q-161640" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-3<x<-1,\\,1<y<0.5x+3\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<x<2,\\,0<y<2\\}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "032fb137-9168-5a99-a5e4-9074a94d7959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465429} {:answer/id #uuid "31c96af2-d123-5df0-997d-6bf01aa71691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "032fb137-9168-5a99-a5e4-9074a94d7959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465429} :answer-field/id #uuid "35c8e728-3d73-591e-810b-c44bf8681591" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :a